<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's LG-Caltex Oil closes CDU for maintenance.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's LG-Caltex Oil closes CDU for maintenance.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's LG-Caltex Oil Corp said it had closed down its No 1 crude distillation unit on Tuesday for an annual maintenance shutdown.</p>
<p>The 100,000 barrel-per-day (bpd) unit is scheduled to resume operation on June 13, it said.</p>
<p>LG-Caltex, the nation's second largest refiner, has a refining capacity of 600,000 bpd.</p>
<p>LG-Caltex is a joint venture between LG Group and Caltex Petroleum Corp, itself a joint venture between U.S. oil giants Texaco Inc and Chevron Corp.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
